# LINE ENDINGS ARE NOT COSMETIC HERE.
#
# This repo had no .gitattributes, so Git's core.autocrlf converts files to CRLF
# on checkout on Windows. Proved in hytek-lws on 07/09/2026, both directions: a
# `.mjs` module with CRLF makes vitest FAIL TO LOAD IT —
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" — while `node --check` and esbuild
# parse the identical bytes without complaint. Worse, vitest blames the file
# that IMPORTED it, so the error points at a comment line in some unrelated test
# and the real cause is invisible.
#
# CI runs on Linux, checks out LF, and is green. So the failure appears only on
# a developer's Windows machine, after a fresh checkout, on code nobody touched.
# That is the worst shape a bug can have: it teaches people that a red local
# suite means nothing.
#
# It matters in THIS repo from Lane 7 CP4 on, which moved the ingest bridge's
# job-number parser into scripts/lib/job-ref.mjs and widened vitest.config.ts to
# run scripts/**/*.test.mjs. Same file type, same trap — closed before anybody
# meets it.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
